      "subject": "fix(native-runtime): treat the desktop shell as non-native",
      "body": "The desktop app is served from a loopback origin (http://127.0.0.1:<port>),\nwhich isLoopbackWebviewOrigin() classifies as native. That made\nisNativeRuntime() return true on desktop, so useAuraCapabilities reported\nisNativeApp/isMobileClient and host-config required an explicit host origin —\nswitching the desktop into the native/mobile UI (wrong login view and shell)\nand changing host resolution.\n\nReturn false from isNativeRuntime() when a desktop bridge global\n(__AURA_BOOT_AUTH__ / __TAURI__ / __TAURI_INTERNALS__) is present, so the\ndesktop is treated as a desktop client while Capacitor and loopback\nmobile-dev webviews stay native.",
